  "towerWide": {
    "_about": "The D6 line heads (owner LM3, LM5): photo style, built from the gauge so the same kit makes any gauge. On the mast cap a box crossarm reaching overhang past each rope; above it a lifting beam on two posts, tied to the crossarm by inclined braces (the trapezoid the photos show); a grated platform with railings along the crossarm's platform side (+u) between the ropes; the mast ladder up through a hatch. Each rope's sheave assembly hangs on lug plates under the crossarm's end, its pin lugs.hang below it, as on the Sessellift kit, so the rope's height at the head follows the head type. Sheave assemblies and head types (s4 ... c8) are the Sessellift kit's (tower.assembly, tower.heads).",
